From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:37:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios: refuse to pack an image the companion's pins were not
 found on
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A game update changes the rewritten main, the module's pinned addresses no
longer hold, and the only symptom is an empty band. build_ipa.sh now checks
the image it embeds — program 0's, the one gen_embed.py links — against the
vendored module's *_pins.inc files before it bundles the companion, and
refuses an image whose build ID is not among companion.json's write_builds:
the pin check proves the addresses, the build gate proves the host will open
the module's domains. The module's directory comes from companion.json's ui,
so the script no longer names acnh.

test_companion_pack.py runs the gate as build_ipa.sh holds it, slicing the
block's text between markers so the test follows the script, over synthetic
images: a matching image, one changed word, a build the host does not open,
an image without its cuts file, and a module without pin files.

Not checked: a full build_ipa.sh run (this NSP folder has no RomFS, host or
font files, so check_program fails before the gate) and lint_python.py (no
venv with the pinned lint requirements on this machine).

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: The ACNH companion's pins: a tool that checks a rewritten image and the pack step that refuses one they were not found on; nxnative carries them on feat/acnh-companion
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion

